      "content": "You should look into variables related to the local population density and the average income level of the neighborhood. Areas with higher concentrations of certain demographic groups, especially those with lower socioeconomic status, often correlate with higher claim frequencies due to different housing quality or maintenance levels. Furthermore, the presence of specific types of local businesses or the age distribution of the residents can serve as useful, albeit indirect, risk indicators.",
